This repository is made public for transparency and so that people can
download and use the app. It is NOT open source.

1. USING THE APP — ALLOWED
   You may download, install and use official builds of Smart Player
   (published on this repository's Releases page) free of charge, for
   personal, non-commercial use, on any number of your own devices.
   You may share links to this repository and its Releases page.

2. THE SOURCE CODE — VIEW ONLY
   You may view and read the source code. Every other right is reserved
   by the copyright holder. Without prior written permission of the
   copyright holder you may NOT:
     a) copy the source code, in whole or in part, into any other project;
     b) modify the source code or create derivative works;
     c) build and distribute your own versions of the app, modified or not;
     d) redistribute the app or its source code (other than by linking to
        this repository), including re-uploading APK files elsewhere;
     e) sell, rent, sublicense or use the app or the code commercially;
     f) publish the app or the code under a different name or author.

   Forking this repository on GitHub is possible because of GitHub's Terms
   of Service, but a fork grants no rights beyond those listed in section 1.

3. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
   The app uses third-party libraries that remain under their own licenses,
   including AndroidX Media3 (Apache License 2.0), Jetpack Compose (Apache
   License 2.0) and FFmpeg (LGPL 2.1 or later) via the Jellyfin
   media3-ffmpeg-decoder build. Nothing in this license restricts your
   rights under those licenses for those components.

4. NO WARRANTY
   The app is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright
   holder is not liable for any damages arising from its use.

For permission requests, open an issue in this repository.

